.\" Man page for f (folder-auto-banner)
.\"
.TH F 1 "2026-06-14" "f 0.6.25" "User Commands"
.\"
.SH NAME
f \- folder-auto-banner: contextual directory dashboard
.\"
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B f
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ PATH ]
.br
.B f banner
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ PATH ]
.RI [ ACTION ]
.br
.B f env
.RI [ PATH ]
.br
.B f install
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.br
.B f config
.br
.B f daemon
.RI { start | restart | stop | status | clear-cache }
.\"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B f
(folder-auto-banner) is a contextual directory dashboard. It combines a file
listing with project signals such as git status, TODO counts, code metrics,
build status, language breakdowns, ports in use, Docker state, and cached test
results.
.PP
Repeated views are served from a background daemon. The first cold view of a
very large directory returns quickly and may show temporary
.B 4.0k
placeholders while directory sizes refresh in the background; subsequent warm
views use populated cached sizes.
.\"
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B f banner
Print the contextual directory dashboard for the current directory or a specific
path.
.TP
.B f env
Output shell aliases for the detected project type.
.TP
.B f install
Install shell wrappers that enable
.B f N
navigation, where
.B N
opens or changes into the numbered item from the banner.
.TP
.B f config
Open the configuration file in the configured editor.
.TP
.B f daemon
Manage the background daemon.
.\"
.SH OPTIONS
.SS General Options
.TP
.BR \-\-help ", " \-h
Display help information.
.TP
.BR \-\-version ", " \-V
Display version information.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Verbose output.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-debug
Debug output.
.TP
.BR \-1 ", " \-\-oneline
Display one entry per line.
.TP
.BR \-\-git\-ignore
Respect .gitignore during traversal.
.TP
.BR \-\-only\-dirs
List only directories.
.TP
.BR \-\-only\-files
List only files.
.TP
.BI \-\-highlight\-recent " MODE"
Background highlight for recent files.
.TP
.BI \-\-highlight\-old " MODE"
Background highlight for old files.
.\"
.SS Banner Options
.TP
.BR \-\-raw ", " \-r
Output raw paths.
.TP
.BR \-\-json
Output JSON.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-compact
Compact output.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-hidden
Show hidden files.
.TP
.BR \-\-classify
Append type indicators.
.TP
.BR \-\-relative\-date
Show relative dates.
.TP
.BI \-\-sort " MODE"
Sort order: name, size, date, type, git, extension, version.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-timesort
Sort by time modified.
.TP
.BR \-S ", " \-\-sizesort
Sort by size.
.TP
.BR \-X ", " \-\-extensionsort
Sort by file extension.
.TP
.BR \-G ", " \-\-gitsort
Sort by git status.
.TP
.BR \-\-versionsort
Natural sort.
.TP
.BR \-U ", " \-\-no\-sort
No sort.
.TP
.BR \-\-reverse
Reverse sort order.
.TP
.BR \-\-group\-dirs \fR=\fIMODE
Group directories: none, first, last.
.TP
.BR \-g ", " \-\-group
Group items by type.
.TP
.BI \-\-filter " PATTERN"
Filter items by glob or extension.
.TP
.BI \-\-ignore\-glob " PATTERN"
Exclude files matching a glob. Can be repeated.
.TP
.BI \-\-max " N"
Maximum number of items to display.
.TP
.BI \-\-level " N"
Limit recursion depth for tree or recursive output.
.TP
.BR \-\-blocks \fR=\fICOLUMNS
Columns to display: permission, owner, group, size, contents, date, name.
.TP
.BR \-\-tree [\fIDEPTH\fR]
Tree view. Depth 0 means unlimited.
.TP
.BR \-\-total\-size
Show total directory size in the header.
.TP
.BR \-\-no\-symlink
Hide symlink targets.
.TP
.BR \-\-hyperlink
Attach terminal hyperlinks to filenames.
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-edit
Force open the selected file in the editor.
.TP
.BR \-x ", " \-\-run
Force run the selected file directly.
.\"
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B f
Show the dashboard for the current directory.
.TP
.B f /path/to/dir
Show the dashboard for a specific directory.
.TP
.B f \-\-json
Output JSON for scripting.
.TP
.B f \-\-raw
Output raw paths for piping.
.TP
.B f \-\-tree
Show a tree view.
.TP
.B f 3
Open or change into item 3 from the banner when shell wrappers are installed.
.TP
.B f 3 cat
Open item 3 with
.BR cat .
.TP
.B f env
Output shell aliases for the current project type.
.TP
.B f config
Open the configuration file.
.TP
.B f daemon status
Show daemon state.
.TP
.B f daemon restart
Restart the daemon.
.\"
.SH CONFIGURATION
The configuration file is located at
.IR ~/.config/fab/config.toml .
.PP
Open it with:
.BR "f config" .
.\"
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disable colors when set.
.TP
.B EDITOR
